          "description": "This employer is hiring for a Junior Java Backend Developer to join their remote team. The role focuses on building robust backend solutions while collaborating with a global technical team.\nThe Role\n• Develop and maintain backend services using Java, ensuring high performance and scalability.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to design and implement RESTful APIs.\n• Participate in technical evaluations and coding assessments to ensure high-quality software delivery.\n• Support the full software development lifecycle, from requirements analysis to implementation.\nWhat You'll Need\n• A Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• 0–2 years of professional experience in Java backend development.\n• Strong foundational knowledge of Data Structures, Algorithms, and Object-Oriented Programming.\n• Ability to work remotely while maintaining availability during Pacific Time (PT) business hours.\nWhat's On Offer\n• Competitive salary\n• Opportunity to work on diverse projects across multiple industry sectors.\n• Exposure to a global, collaborative professional environment.\nApply via Haystack today!",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483241529": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:53:25.093092+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Razor is seeking several Junior Java Developer to support the development, testing, deployment, and maintenance of enterprise applications. This position offers an early-career developer the opportunity to gain hands-on experience with Java-based applications, collaborate with senior developers, and contribute to software solutions in an Agile environment.\nClearance Requirements\n- Must be able to obtain a VA Medium Background Investigation.\nKey Responsibilities\nDevelop, test, deploy, and maintain Java-based applications under the guidance of senior developers.\nAnalyze customer requirements and assist in developing software solutions that align with existing system architecture and operating environments.\nWrite, debug, and enhance software code for new and existing applications.\nSupport application troubleshooting, maintenance, and ongoing enhancements.\nWork with REST and SOAP web services, relational databases, and associated application technologies.\nParticipate in Agile development activities, software testing, and code reviews.\nCollaborate with senior developers and technical teams on application design and delivery.\nDevelop and maintain software documentation.\nSupport development activities across Windows and web-based environments.\nRequired Qualifications\n1–2 years of professional Java development experience.\nUnderstanding of object-oriented programming, software development fundamentals, and system architecture.\nExperience developing, testing, debugging, deploying, or supporting Java-based applications.\nExperience with some of the following technologies: Spring, REST APIs, SOAP Web Services, JavaScript, AngularJS, jQuery, Oracle, SQL, WebLogic, JPA/Hibernate, or Java EE.\nFamiliarity with Agile software development methodologies.\nUnderstanding of relational database management systems.\nAbility to analyze technical requirements, troubleshoot application issues, and develop effective software solutions.\nStrong problem-solving, communication, and collaboration skills.\nPreferred Qualifications\nExperience with service-oriented architecture concepts and enabling technologies.\nExperience with rule engines and Business Process Management (BPM) engines.\nExperience with Rational Tool Suite.\nEmployer Information\nRazor is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic.\nBenefits Overview\nRazor offers a comprehensive benefits package that may include medical, dental, and vision insurance; life and disability insurance; paid time off and holidays; a 401(k) plan; and professional development opportunities. Benefits offerings may vary based on position and employment status.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483264425": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:53:25.093092+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Location: Remote\nEmployment Type: Full-Time\nExperience Level: Mid-Level (3–5+ years)\nWork Schedule: Monday – Friday, 7:00 AM – 4:00 PM US Central Time\nCompany : Better It for Less\nRole: Full Stack Developer (WordPress | Laravel | React.js | Next.js)\nAbout the Role\nWe are looking for Full Stack Developer with strong frontend and backend development capabilities.\nThe ideal candidate should be able to independently develop websites, web applications, dashboards, and custom software solution, from understanding requirements and designing database architecture to development, testing, and deployment.\nWe value developers who are technically strong, have a good sense of UI/UX, actively use AI-powered development tools, and can quickly adapt to new technologies.\nKey Responsibilities\nConvert Figma designs into responsive, visually accurate WordPress websites using Elementor and custom development.\nBuild modern web applications using React.js, Next.js, JavaScript, and TypeScript.\nDevelop scalable and secure backend applications using PHP and Laravel.\nDesign database schemas, relationships, migrations, and optimized queries.\nWork with MySQL, PostgreSQL (PGSQL), SQLite, and Supabase.\nDevelop and integrate REST APIs, third-party services, authentication systems, and payment gateways.\nCustomize WordPress themes, plugins, Elementor components, and dynamic functionality.\nBuild admin dashboards, internal tools, and custom business applications.\nIndependently debug, optimize, maintain, and deploy applications.\nUse AI development tools to accelerate coding, debugging, research, and automation while reviewing the quality and security of generated code.\nEnsure responsive design, application performance, security, and maintainable code.\nResearch and implement new technologies based on project requirements.\nRequired Technical Skills\n1. Frontend Development\nStrong HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, and responsive design skills.\nHands-on experience with React.js and Next.js.\nFamiliarity with TypeScript and Tailwind CSS.\nAbility to translate Figma designs into functional interfaces.\nGood understanding of UI/UX fundamentals, typography, spacing, and visual consistency.\n2. WordPress & Website Builder Development\nStrong hands-on experience with WordPress and Elementor.\nProven Figma-to-WordPress conversion experience.\nExperience building, customizing, and maintaining websites using Squarespace.\nAbility to customize Squarespace templates, layouts, styling, and website functionality.\nWordPress theme and plugin customization.\nCustom PHP, CSS, and JavaScript implementation.\nExperience with dynamic content, custom post types, and integrations.\nAbility to troubleshoot and optimize WordPress and Squarespace websites.\n3. Backend Development\nStrong PHP and Laravel development experience.\nREST API development and integration.\nAuthentication, authorization, and role-based access control.\nBackend architecture, business logic, and data validation.\nThird-party API integrations, webhooks, and background jobs.\nApplication security, error handling, and performance optimization.\n4. Database Development\nExperience with MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and Supabase.\nAbility to design complete database schemas independently.\nStrong SQL query-writing and optimization skills.\nUnderstanding of relationships, indexing, constraints, and migrations.\nExperience with Supabase authentication and database security.\n5. Development Tools & Deployment\nGit and GitHub.\nAI coding assistants such as ChatGPT, Cursor, or GitHub Copilot.\nAPI testing tools such as Postman.\nBasic Linux/server management.\nDeployment, hosting, and environment configuration.\nFamiliarity with testing, debugging, and CI/CD workflows.\nAdditional Skills (Good to Have)\nWooCommerce and headless WordPress.\nNode.js and Express.js.\nDocker, Redis, and caching.\nAWS, Vercel, or other cloud deployment platforms.\nAutomated testing using PHPUnit, Pest, Vitest, or Playwright.\nTechnical SEO, accessibility, and Core Web Vitals.\nExperience integrating AI APIs into applications.\nExperience building SaaS products, CRM systems, or internal automation tools.\nKey Qualities We Are Looking For\nEnd-to-end ownership: Capable of handling complete features independently.\nStrong problem-solving: Can investigate technical issues and find practical solutions.\nDesign awareness: Has an eye for clean, modern, user-friendly interfaces.\nBackend strength: Understands application architecture beyond basic CRUD operations.\nAI-first productivity: Uses AI tools effectively without compromising code quality.\nAdaptability: Comfortable exploring unfamiliar technologies and frameworks.\nAccountability: Delivers reliable, maintainable, production-ready applications.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483635899": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:53:25.093092+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Company\nParsons is a digitally enabled solutions provider with nearly 75 years of experience, specializing in defense, security, and infrastructure markets. We deliver cutting-edge cyber and converged security solutions, technology-based intellectual property, and innovative services to federal, regional, and local government agencies, as well as private industrial customers worldwide. Our Federal Solutions segment supports critical missions globally by providing resources and expertise in defense, intelligence, infrastructure, and environmental sectors. We foster a culture of excellence, innovation, and collaboration, empowering our employees to contribute to impactful projects that protect and sustain our nation’s most vital assets.\nAbout The Role\nParsons is seeking a talented Front End Software Engineer to join our dynamic team. In this role, you will be responsible for developing and maintaining frontend software applications using JavaScript, React, TypeScript, and Next.js. You will work closely with cross-functional teams in an Agile/Scrum environment to enhance application usability and user experience. Your contributions will include designing, testing, debugging, and delivering high-quality software. Additionally, you will participate in pair programming, peer reviews, and sprint planning sessions, while supporting automated testing and troubleshooting production issues. This position offers the opportunity to work remotely with occasional travel and requires an active Secret security clearance.\nQualifications\nBachelor's Degree in Computer Science or related field, or equivalent experience (minimum 5 years)\nActive Secret security clearance (mandatory)\nProficiency in JavaScript, React, TypeScript, and Next.js\nExperience with Git and modern version control workflows\nStrong background in developing and maintaining frontend applications\nExperience working in Agile/Scrum development environments\nExcellent collaboration skills including pair programming and peer reviews\nStrong troubleshooting, problem-solving, and communication skills\nDesired qualifications include experience with:\nAutomated end-to-end testing frameworks such as Cypress\nJest, React Testing Library, unit and integration testing\nMaterial UI or similar frontend component libraries\nCI/CD pipelines and DevSecOps practices\nContainerization and orchestration tools like Docker and Kubernetes\nCloud platforms such as AWS, Platform One, or DAF CLOUDworks\nBackend technologies including Java, Spring Boot, Node.js, or Python\nData technologies such as PostgreSQL, Liquibase, SPARQL, Elasticsearch, or Logstash\nSecurity concepts including OAuth, JWT, OWASP principles, secure coding, CVEs, and penetration testing\nExperience using Jira for issue tracking and management\nSupporting government, Air Force, COMSEC, CCI, or cryptographic systems\nResponsibilities\nDevelop and maintain frontend software applications using JavaScript, React, TypeScript, and Next.js\nImplement enhancements to improve application usability and user experience\nDesign, develop, test, debug, and maintain software throughout the development lifecycle\nCollaborate with engineers and cross-functional teams in an Agile/Scrum environment\nParticipate in pair programming, peer reviews, backlog refinement, and sprint planning\nInvestigate and resolve software defects and troubleshoot production issues\nContribute to automated frontend testing development and maintenance\nSupport software release quality and related testing activities\nDocument software, processes, and technical solutions as appropriate\nWork effectively as part of a fully remote team with occasional travel requirements\nBenefits\nCompetitive salary range of $103,500 to $181,100\nComprehensive medical, dental, and vision insurance\nPaid time off and holidays to support work-life balance\n401(k) retirement savings plan\nLife insurance coverage\nFlexible work schedules\nOpportunities for professional growth and career advancement\nSupportive and inclusive work environment\nEqual Opportunity\nParsons is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other protected status. We are committed to fostering diversity and inclusion in the workplace and encourage applicants from all backgrounds to apply.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483745239": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:53:25.093092+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Title: Junior Software Developer\nType: Full-time\nLocation: Remote\nExperience: 0–2 Years\nJob Summary:\nWe are seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Junior Software Developer to support the development, maintenance, and enhancement of software applications used in pharmaceutical, biotechnology, and life sciences environments. The ideal candidate will contribute to application development, database management, software testing, and technical documentation while learning how digital solutions support laboratory operations, pharmaceutical manufacturing, clinical research, and quality management. This role is suitable for recent graduates with a background in life sciences or technology who are interested in applying software development skills to scientific and healthcare-related business processes.\nKey Responsibilities:\nApplication Development: Assist in designing, developing, and maintaining software applications that support laboratory workflows, pharmaceutical operations, quality processes, and internal business requirements.\nProgramming and Coding: Write, review, and debug basic code using programming languages such as Python, Java, C#, or JavaScript under the guidance of experienced developers.\nDatabase Management: Support database queries, data retrieval, record updates, and basic database maintenance using SQL and relational database concepts.\nSoftware Testing: Develop and execute basic test cases, document test results, identify software defects, and assist with resolving reported issues.\nApplication Troubleshooting: Investigate application errors, review logs, reproduce technical issues, and escalate complex problems to senior development or support teams.\nSystem Integration: Assist with integrating software applications with databases, reporting tools, laboratory information systems, or other approved enterprise platforms.\nLife Sciences Workflow Support: Learn and document business workflows associated with laboratory testing, sample tracking, inventory management, manufacturing records, and quality documentation.\nTechnical Documentation: Prepare and maintain code documentation, application specifications, user guides, release notes, and technical support records.\nVersion Control: Use version-control tools such as Git to manage code changes, track development progress, and collaborate with other developers.\nComputerized System Compliance: Support software testing and documentation activities for systems used in regulated environments, following applicable procedures and validation requirements.\nData Security: Follow established access controls, confidentiality requirements, and data protection practices when working with scientific, operational, or business information.\nCross-Functional Collaboration: Work with business analysts, quality teams, laboratory personnel, validation specialists, and other developers to understand requirements and deliver reliable software solutions.\nRequired Skills:\nBachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Biotechnology, Bioinformatics, Life Sciences, Computational Biology, Biomedical Engineering, or a related discipline .\nBasic understanding of programming concepts, data structures, debugging, and software development fundamentals.\nFamiliarity with at least one programming language, such as Python, Java, C#, or JavaScript.\nBasic knowledge of SQL, relational databases, and data handling.\nUnderstanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) concepts, including requirements, development, testing, deployment, and maintenance.\nFamiliarity with software testing, defect tracking, and technical documentation.\nAwareness of version-control tools such as Git is an advantage.\nBasic understanding of pharmaceutical or life sciences workflows is preferred.\nAwareness of Good Documentation Practices (GDP), data integrity, and computerized system validation (CSV) concepts is beneficial.\nStrong analytical thinking, problem-solving, attention to detail, and willingness to learn.\nGood written and verbal communication skills.\nPreferred: Academic projects, internships, or practical exposure to application development, database projects, bioinformatics tools, laboratory software, or digital solutions for pharmaceutical operations.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4483751954": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:53:25.093092+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "What You’ll Be Doing\nCadmus is seeking a Junior Full Stack Developer to join our Federal Operations Group. This role provides full-stack software development support to a file management application team, a high-performing Agile team responsible for delivering enterprise platforms and shared services that support multiple systems at a federal government health care organization. This solution includes file management activities including uploading and downloading files for a major federal healthcare organization. Other functionalities include large file transfers, file workflows, anti-virus scanning, PHI/PII scanning and other capabilities related to the secure transfer of files. It is anticipated that this file management application will undergo a complete redesign in the next few months.\nWho We Are\nCadmus provides government, commercial, and other private organizations worldwide with technology-empowered advisory and implementation services. We help our clients achieve their goals and drive lasting, impactful change by leveraging transformative digital solutions and unparalleled expertise across domains.\nAt Cadmus, we look for team players and problem solvers who are driven to use their unique perspectives and intellectual curiosity to help deliver breakthrough solutions that achieve transformative goals. As a member of our team, you'll collaborate with leading experts to support our clients across the globe. We offer competitive compensation, outstanding health care and retirement benefits, a vibrant and collaborative work environment, and ample opportunities for professional growth.\nJoin Cadmus. Together, we are strengthening society and the natural world. For more information, visit cadmusgroup.com .\nResponsibilities\n1–2 years of hands-on experience building and maintaining web applications using modern frontend and backend technologies.\nCollaborate with senior developers, product owners, and DevOps engineers to design, develop, test, and deploy scalable applications on cloud infrastructure.\nDevelop responsive and interactive user interfaces using Angular and /or React.\nDesign, develop, and maintain backend services using Python and/or JavaScript (NodeJS).\nDesign, implement, and integrate REST APIs with frontend applications and third-party services.\nDeploy, configure, and maintain applications on AWS cloud services.\nWork in Linux environments for application deployment, troubleshooting, and automation.]\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-documented code following coding standards.\nParticipate in code reviews, debugging, testing, and performance optimization.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams using Agile/Scrum methodologies.\nTroubleshoot production issues and assist in maintaining application availability.\nQualifications\nBachelor’s degree in computer science, Information Technology, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience).\n1–2 years of experience in full stack web development - Python, JavaScript, NodeJS\nExperience with relational databases (PostgreSQL, MySQL, or similar).\nProficiency with Git and collaborative development workflows.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD pipelines (Jenkins CJE) and DevOps practices.\nExperience with Docker and Kubernetes.\nKnowledge of HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript/TypeScript.\nKnowledge of automated testing frameworks and test-driven development.\nComfortable in stepping out of the comfort zone to suggest, test, implement new technologies and frameworks.\nAbility to independently research and suggest solutions for ongoing improvement including new frameworks and infrastructure requirements.\nA passion for scaling software, ensuring high availability enjoyment of automation and demonstrate a proactive approach to detecting and resolving issues.\nMust be a self-starter\nStrong communication skills - both written and verbal. The ability to articulate ideas to non-technical audience.\nAgile oriented in approach to engineering and operations, including being comfortable with ambiguity in a flat organization.\nBelieve in a quick improvement approach: Fail fast, learn fast, improve fast.\nPreferred Skills\nAdded project-relevant areas such as S3, ECS/Fargate, SQS, EventBridge, API Gateway, IAM, KMS, RBAC, secure APIs, and file-processing security.\nExperience with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform or CloudFormation).\nFamiliarity with messaging systems such as Kafka, or Amazon SQS.\nExperience implementing authentication and authorization (OAuth2, JWT, SAML).\nFamiliarity with monitoring and logging tools.\nKnowledge of security best-practices for web applications.\nExperience working in a DevOps-oriented environment.\nConfigure and manage Nginx as a web server and reverse proxy or has experience with similar technologies like Tomcat, Apache.\nFamiliarity with AI Assisted coding practices/tools (Co-Pilot, Cursor etc.).\nAdditional Information\nCandidates must be eligible to work in the United States as a U.S Perm Resident or U.S. Citizen.\nBased on eligibility and job status, Cadmus offers an excellent benefits package to include: medical, dental, vision, company paid disability and life insurance, 401(k) program, paid time off (PTO), paid holidays, voluntary time off (VTO), tuition reimbursement, adoption assistance program, other optional benefits and various bonus programs.\nThe salary range for this position is $80,000 - $100,000. The actual salary will be determined by several factors, including relevant work experience, education, skills, and market competitiveness.\nWe value the critical role safety and health protocols contribute to everyone’s success at Cadmus, and work together to align and comply with all federal, state, and local safety and health mandates to ensure a safe and valuable work environment.\nCadmus is an Equal Opportunity Employer and prohibits unlawful discrimination. Cadmus is committed to providing a respectful workplace where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants and employees without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation (including gender identity and/or expression), national origin, military and veteran status, physical and mental disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\nLearn more about Cadmus by visiting our website at: cadmusgroup.com .",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4484213042": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:53:25.093092+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About Contour\nContour Software has grown from a dozen people to over 2,000 staff across 3 cities, in less than 14 years.\nAs a subsidiary of Constellation Software Inc., we are proud to be part of a global enterprise software conglomerate that has grown to become one of the top 10 software companies in the world, with employees and customers in 100+ countries. With a broad-based and ever-growing portfolio of market-leading, vertical-market enterprise solutions covering more than 100 industry domains in predominantly mature markets, CSI's recipe creates the perfect environment for professionals to build fulfilling, long-term careers.\nWhat started as an R&D & Accounting back-office, has progressed into a full-service Global Centre serving all functions and departments, at the divisional as well as operating group/corporate level. Today Contour employees, located in Karachi, Lahore & Islamabad, are serving CSI divisions located in time zones spanning the globe, from Sydney to Vancouver. With the global growth of Constellation as the wind in our sails, we are only just getting started!\nThe Position\nWe are looking for Trainee Software Developers to join one of our R&D teams. The selected candidates will be trained for 3 to 3.5 months to become good developers capable of working on enterprise-level applications. After the end of the internship period, there is a good possibility of full-time employment based on satisfactory performance during the internship.\nThe chosen individuals will work out of the Contour Software Karachi resource center office, as an extension of the division-based R&D department.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nBS/MS in Computer Science or related field.\nExcellent communication skills in English.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming principles.\nGood programming concepts and knowledge of Java or C#.\nStrong competencies in data structures, algorithms, and software design.\nComfortable with SQL and basic database development concepts.\nExposure to Generative AI, LLMs, RAG, Prompt Engineering, or AI-powered application development.\nGood knowledge of frontend programming with JavaScript, Angular, React, React Native, Blazor, or Vue.js.\nKnowledge of REST APIs.\nExperience and knowledge of Git.\nA quick learner, with attention to detail, and a commitment to meeting deadlines.\nKnowledge of professional software engineering practices\nGood verbal and non-verbal communication skills.\nDisclaimer: At Contour, we attribute our success to the unique contributions of our diverse staff. We’re committed to fostering a culture of respect that thrives on the varied perspectives and experiences of all individuals we recruit, employ, promote, and compensate. Since day one, we’ve adhered to a policy that champions a work environment honoring the worth and dignity of each person while being free from all forms of employment discrimination.\nIn our continuous effort to promote inclusivity, we extend our commitment to individuals with special needs by providing reasonable accommodations. We actively encourage qualified individuals with special needs to apply for the various openings within our company. Should you require assistance in completing the application process or have any inquiries regarding special facilities, please do not hesitate to contact our HR team. Your unique talents and abilities are welcomed and valued here.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4318354760": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:04:35.875414+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Are you passionate about creating robust and scalable software solutions?<br><br>Join us as a <strong>Full Stack Developer</strong> and play a key role in building impactful applications. We’re looking for someone with a strong technical background, problem-solving mindset, and collaborative attitude to help shape our innovative projects.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities<br><br></strong><ul><li> Design, develop, and implement scalable software applications using C# and .NET Core.</li><li> Build and optimize Web APIs with a focus on best practices.</li><li> Work with JavaScript, jQuery, and other front-end technologies to deliver seamless user experiences.</li><li> Write clean, efficient, and maintainable code with a focus on performance and scalability.</li><li> Collaborate with developers, product managers, and stakeholders to deliver new features and enhancements.</li><li> Troubleshoot, debug and upgrade the software to ensure optimal functionality.</li><li> Lead by example, providing technical guidance and mentorship to the team.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Qualifications<br><br></strong><ul><li> Education: Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or a related field.</li><li> Experience: 2 years of hands-on experience in software development, including front-end and back-end work.</li><li> Technical Skills:</li><li> Strong expertise in C#, .NET Core, MVC, and Microservices architecture.</li><li> Proficiency in JavaScript, jQuery, and other front-end frameworks.</li><li> Knowledge of database management and integration.</li><li> Soft Skills:</li><li> Excellent verbal and written communication skills.</li><li> Strong analytical, problem-solving, and organizational abilities.</li><li> A collaborative team player with a proactive attitude.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Why Join Us?<br><br></strong><ul><li> Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits.</li><li> Performance bonuses based on your contributions and team achievements.</li><li> The opportunity to work on industry-leading projects.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Location:</strong> This is a <strong>full-time, onsite role</strong> based in Karachi."
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481855208": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-10-27T18:04:35.875414+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Title: ServiceNow Service Mapping Practitioner (ITOM)*<br>*Location: Remote - West Coast Client (US Hours)*<br>*Experience: 4+ Years (ITOM Preferred)*<br>*Engagement Type: Contract*<br><br>### About The Role<br>We are looking for an experienced ServiceNow Service Mapping Practitioner with a strong focus on ITOM and AIOps. The ideal candidate will be responsible for improving infrastructure visibility and mapping complex application dependencies across enterprise environments.<br><br>### Key Responsibilities<br><br>*ServiceNow ITOM &amp; Discovery:*<br>- Design, implement, and manage Application Service Mapping (Top-down service maps) and Horizontal Discovery.<br>- Manage Discovery Schedules, Credentials, and MID Servers.<br>- Create and modify Discovery Patterns as per business requirements.<br>- Troubleshoot Discovery and Pattern-related issues.<br><br>*CMDB &amp; Platform:*<br>- Ensure CMDB health, data integrity, and governance.<br>- Work on Integration with Event Management and CMDB.<br>- Leverage IntegrationHub &amp; Flow Designer for automation and integrations.<br>- Develop and consume REST/SOAP APIs.<br><br>*Technical Skills:*<br>- Proficient in Scripting: JavaScript, PowerShell, Bash, or Regex.<br>- Strong understanding of Azure, Networking, and Operating System layers (Windows/Linux).<br><br>### Required Qualifications<br>- 4+ years of hands-on experience in ServiceNow ITOM.<br>- Strong expertise in Service Mapping and Discovery.<br>- CIS-Service Mapping and CIS-Discovery certifications are *strongly preferred*.<br><br>### What We Offer<br>- Remote opportunity working with a West Coast enterprise client.<br>- Contract engagement with opportunity to work on large-scale ITOM/AIOps transformation.<br><br>*Interested?*<br>If this opportunity aligns with your experience, please share your updated resume and your availability for a quick discussion."
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4481863008": {
